Scope of the MIT licence
------------------------
The MIT License in LICENSE covers Zonked's original code, documentation and
original templates. It does not cover the items in parts A and B below. Each
of those keeps its own terms.

A. Shipped third-party material (inside the built app)

1. Font. Atkinson Hyperlegible Next (latin 400 and 700, woff2), copyright The
   Atkinson Hyperlegible Next Project Authors. SIL Open Font License 1.1. The
   licence text is in web/public/fonts/OFL.txt and must travel with every copy
   of the font files.

2. Nature loops. 22 short loops in web/public/samples/, cut and re-encoded from
   recordings by their authors (21 distinct sources). Each is CC0 1.0 or put in
   the public domain by its author. Every file, author, source page, licence
   and hash is listed in docs/SAMPLES-LICENSES.md. Saved copies of the source
   pages for the public domain files are in docs/legal/samples/. Thank you to
   the recording authors, even where the licence does not ask for credit. To
   report a file, see the takedown section in docs/SAMPLES-LICENSES.md.

3. Runtime code. React and React DOM (MIT, Meta Platforms and contributors) in
   the web app (version 19) and in the Kiro Crew app UI (version 18). The
   service worker is generated with Workbox (MIT, Google and contributors) by
