B. Reference material that is not shipped

5. legacy/android
   "Binaural Beats Therapy" by Giorgio Regni, an Android app published as the
   GitHub project GiorgioRegni/Binaural-Beats. GNU General Public License
   version 3, full text in legacy/android/LICENSE. These files are Giorgio
   Regni's work and stay under the GPLv3. They are kept for reference only.
   The app does not import, compile, bundle or ship them.

6. legacy/gnaural
   Three binaural beat schedules in the Gnaural XML format (Power Nap, a
   meditation schedule for airplane travel, and "Arrive sharp"). Each file
   names Gnaural as its source and carries no licence text. They came with the
   GPLv3 Android app above. Their terms are unknown, so treat them as
   third-party reference material. Gnaural is free software published under
   the GPL.

C. Credits and lineage

7. Inspiration. Zonked credits three sources of ideas: SBaGen (1998), the
   `.sbg` brainwave sequence idea, with no SBaGen code used; Gnaural, for
   binaural beat schedules; and Giorgio Regni's Android app. The author's 2018
   final-year web application, its research and its yellow mask mascot were
   made after studying that Android app.

8. The 24 seed templates. These 24 templates in web/src/catalog/seeds.ts
   (ids that start with seed-) used to follow the step tables of the Android
   app and of the Gnaural files. They are now original schedules written for
   Zonked, with new ids and source "original". Saved favorites that used the
   old ids are moved to the new ids when they are read (web/src/catalog/
   legacyIds.ts). The Android app, the Gnaural files and SBaGen stay credited
   as inspiration in item 7, and the reference copies in legacy/ stay where
   they are, unshipped. LAWYER: whether the earlier release history of this
   repository needs any statement about the old tables, and the final wording
   of this item. Nothing here is a legal opinion.

